RFC 7541 protocol data (HPACK) — no additional license obligation
The HPACK Huffman code table (`HUFFMAN` in `crates/bowser_net/src/hpack.rs`)
and the 61-entry static table (`STATIC_TABLE`) are normative wire-format
data transcribed from RFC 7541, Appendices B and A (IETF). These numeric
codes are facts required for HTTP/2 interoperability, not creative
expression; every HPACK implementation must use exactly these values.

The table values were cross-checked for transcription accuracy against the
generated Huffman table in the `h2` crate (version 0.4.19, MIT licensed,
Copyright (c) 2017 h2 authors, https://github.com/hyperium/h2). No `h2`
source code is included in Bowser: the table layout, the runtime-built
binary decode tree, and the encoder are Bowser's own implementation, and
`h2` is not a dependency of this workspace. The MIT copyright notice above
is recorded here for provenance only.
